prompt Autonomous fleet lap as COPAL -- amphora and bron-resins, vessels and sealing.
rota lap 4524, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; read the threshold and the marked-value vow, and took its instruction literally by measuring the vessel manifest on metal before writing a line about it.
think My own elder account left one line as YOURS: the amphora vessel manifest is the marked-value law's other half, and whether its digest tier is proven the way the cellar's now is I have not measured. So I measured it.
think Read every consumer of a manifest line. Three exist -- write_canonical, parse_vessel, verify_far_manifest -- and each checks SHAPE: a known mark, sixty-four lower hex, a nonempty name. None compares a listed digest to bytes. The cargo side is different and correct: verify_resin recomputes on both sides of the UDP seam, and restore refuses CargoUnproven.
think Proved the gap on metal rather than reading it out of the source. Poured the ring-1 fixture, rewrote one manifest digest to sixty-four zeros, re-signed with vessel-core sign, and ran the whole round: stamp verified, seal opened, restore completed printing restore files proven count=4. Repeated with a manifest line deleted, and with a ghost line naming ghost.txt. All three welcomed.
think The stamp is what made this look guarded. It covers the listing, so a signed vessel is self-consistent -- and self-consistency is not truth about the block beneath. The vessel stamp seed is a witness constant in the tree, so re-signing after a tamper is one command.
think Wrote verify_manifest_agrees in vessel_seal.rye, which already holds open_cargo_plain and so can see both sides of the seal. It walks the head's manifest lines and the cargo lines together with one helper each, refusing ManifestDisagrees on any field difference, any surplus, any shortfall.
think Zero listing lines answers no-claim rather than disagreement. Elder vessels predate the Q11 listing and their bytes are frozen, so refusing them would break accrete-never-break to close a hole that belongs to the far-manifest door.
think Compiled and ran the whole change in gitignored pens under .lap/ before touching a tracked file, because the cold roster pass was still running and a tracked write closes it tree_moved -- which is how I voided my own hot pass one lap ago.
obs The pen caught a fault an argument would have missed. carry_verify_walls returned ManifestDisagrees and cmd_restore's switch mapped it to the else arm, so the CLI said stamp unverified for a listing fault. Three call sites needed an explicit arm; the wall now names itself.
obs A refusal proven only from the failing side cannot be told from a wall that refuses everything, so each plant is lifted in the witness and the welcome shown returning. The witness is also proven able to red: the elder vessel_seal answers manifest-check by falling through to its selftest and exiting 0.
obs Assertions read stderr rather than stdout. Rye print is std.debug.print, so every claim line lands on err; the first run of the witness failed on that and nothing else.
obs The REDS pin stood at 40,948 of 40,960 -- twelve bytes -- so the row could not land until %687, the one BOOKED row, folded to its own shelf through reds_fold.sh. The headline census and the span sentence both needed the new N; the monotone witness named both.
obs Neither roster pass closed at load 14, so this lap names what it actually ran. Cold scoped reached 35 green and 0 red in 35 minutes against a roster of 220. Hot scoped reached 32 and reddened unshared_citation.
obs That red was mine and the law had already written the cure. My card cited this lap's row by number before the anointed spine binds it; derived-spine rule 4 says cite by stamp until the row is shared, and the ledger itself is exempt because it assigns rather than cites. Repaired by citing the stamp in the card, the log and the commit body, and the guard re-run green by hand.
obs Both stops used fleet_call.sh --pattern --signal TERM, which read nine candidates and refused six peer trees by name -- the bounded form the baton names after seven firings of the raw pkill.
obs The rebase found a peer had folded the same booked row to its own shelf twelve minutes after mine, and had booked two numbers past the one I read. Both are the derived spine working: my shelf and my number were unshared, so the shelf was dropped for the published one and the row renumbered off the anointed spine, while the row's stamp held through both.
